# USE WHEN implementing planning strategies, optimizing planning patterns, or enhancing documentation structure

# Planning Patterns Guide

## Overview

This guide provides comprehensive documentation for the new planning patterns implemented in the system-wide plan-mode enhancement. These patterns enable more effective planning for large documentation files, intelligent folder structuring, and optimized tool usage.

## Tool-Aware File Reading Patterns

### When to Use

Use these patterns when:
- Working with large documentation files (>250 lines)
- Needing to maintain context across multiple file reads
- Implementing documentation with clear section boundaries
- Optimizing tool calls for complex planning tasks

### Implementation Approaches

#### Size-Based Reading Strategy

```typescript
// Before reading a file, check its size
function checkFileSize(file: string): ReadingStrategy {
  const estimatedSize = estimateFileSize(file);
  
  if (estimatedSize <= 250) {
    return {
      strategy: 'whole_file',
      params: { should_read_entire_file: true }
    };
  } else if (estimatedSize <= 750) {
    return {
      strategy: 'single_chunk',
      params: { offset: 0, limit: estimatedSize }
    };
  } else {
    return {
      strategy: 'multi_chunk',
      params: calculateOptimalChunks(estimatedSize)
    };
  }
}

// Read file with appropriate strategy
async function readWithStrategy(file: string): Promise<string> {
  const strategy = checkFileSize(file);
  
  if (strategy.strategy === 'whole_file') {
    return read_file(file, should_read_entire_file=true);
  } else if (strategy.strategy === 'single_chunk') {
    return read_file(file, strategy.params.offset, strategy.params.limit);
  } else {
    // Multi-chunk reading
    const chunks = [];
    for (const chunk of strategy.params) {
      chunks.push(await read_file(file, chunk.offset, chunk.limit));
    }
    return combineChunks(chunks);
  }
}
```

#### Section-Based Reading Strategy

```typescript
// Read file by logical sections
async function readBySection(file: string, targetSection: string): Promise<string> {
  // First scan to find sections
  const initialContent = await read_file(file, 0, 250);
  const sections = findSections(initialContent);
  
  // Locate target section
  const targetSectionInfo = sections.find(s => s.title.includes(targetSection));
  if (!targetSectionInfo) {
    return initialContent; // Section not found in first chunk
  }
  
  // Read target section
  return read_file(file, targetSectionInfo.startLine, targetSectionInfo.lineCount);
}
```

